{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "024S", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-topological-unramified}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b56490d7030e360eb7429fffcc8c1c5d0c66df7c1a9800d565c9e60a8a4b790f", "source_text": "Topological properties of unramified morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:03c16c7f31ad3d64e32057d918a711e68f0561db53b788ff935459a26d2d76f5", "unit_id": "tag:024S:title"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "024S", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:efce62362620cd2904bedf6a039209048d9b541be7f9a3e63f0ee0a26cf3f58a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe first topological result that will be of utility to us is one which says\nthat unramified and separated morphisms have ``nice'' sections.\nThe material in this section does not require any Noetherian hypotheses.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3ad69d095a01611c8ec4cee6b2c85728a42cc76788705446cc60de958cf18a5f", "unit_id": "tag:024S:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proposition", "parent_tag": "024S", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proposition}\n\\label{proposition-properties-sections}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proposition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:84fbea2a09fc695bdaef30449f9e9ffef6da80d28a3bc3c8f4ee1ed61732275f", "source_text": "Sections of unramified morphisms.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Any section of an unramified morphism is an open immersion.\n<STRUCT_0003> Any section of a separated morphism is a closed immersion.\n<STRUCT_0004> Any section of an unramified separated morphism is open and closed.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f909c4fe2bace6a1db3e534fa44127a9c63be88a18691fd41424f37119df6e8a", "unit_id": "tag:024T:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "024S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X' \\to X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Gamma_f : X' \\to X' \\times_S X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Delta_{X/S} : X \\to X \\times_S X$", "MATH_0006": "$X' \\times_S X \\to X \\times_S X$", "MATH_0007": "$g : X \\to S$", "MATH_0008": "$X' = S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-definition-separated}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-diagonal-unramified-morphism}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-base-change-immersion}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:519277c9d4f3713ab1b7d1131dee47b7dacc442d7be6048e71483272633472c6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:890d7748bcddf2f71f8317cb752419354328c60f00203f257210d09f020ae566", "source_text": "Fix a base scheme <MATH_0001>.\nIf <MATH_0002> is any <MATH_0003>-morphism, then the graph\n<MATH_0004>\nis obtained as the base change of the diagonal\n<MATH_0005> via the projection\n<MATH_0006>.\nIf <MATH_0007> is separated (resp. unramified)\nthen the diagonal is a closed immersion (resp. open immersion)\nby Schemes, Definition <REF_0001>\n(resp.<SPACE_0001>Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nHence so is the graph as a base change (by\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0003>).\nIn the special case <MATH_0008>, we obtain (1), resp.<SPACE_0002>(2).\nPart (3) follows on combining (1) and (2).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a596bd7e74f874323413508332f84146bee8698a8823e3d32394b639f2c3ddfd", "unit_id": "tag:024T:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "024S", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:efce62362620cd2904bedf6a039209048d9b541be7f9a3e63f0ee0a26cf3f58a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe can now explicitly describe the sections of unramified morphisms.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:694b3aa1fc255a61523eb212f420800130f9191f6432dc448a39e1d692653daa", "unit_id": "tag:024S:prose-0002"}
